# Multi-taper Schur continuation — what is kernel-checked here

This note records, precisely, the status of the multi-taper Schur architecture
inside *this* project.  It exists because the architecture was first described in a
report produced in an environment with no Lean toolchain, where the described files
could not be typechecked and are not present in this repository.  Everything listed
below was (re)implemented here and **verified by the pinned Lean toolchain**:
`lake build Zeta23Bridge` succeeds, and every theorem named here reports axioms
`[propext, Classical.choice, Quot.sound]` under `#print axioms`.

There are no `sorry`, `admit`, `axiom`, `postulate` or `@[implemented_by]`
declarations in any module added by this tranche.

